# Spring Boot / Java 25 - apptdea & banktdea

Apply these conventions on every change in this project:

## Stack
- Java 21 / Java 25 modern features (Records, Pattern Matching, Sealed Classes, Virtual Threads)
- Spring Boot 4.x / 3.x with Maven
- Package base: `com.udea.apptdea` and `com.udea.banktdea`
- Data: Spring Data JPA + PostgreSQL (with in-memory H2 dev profile fallback)
- API docs: springdoc-openapi (Swagger UI)

## Naming Conventions (Always in English)
- Classes, interfaces, methods, fields, parameters, packages, and constants: **English only**.
- Controllers: `*Controller`
- Services: `*Service` / `*ServiceImpl`
- Repositories: `*Repository`
- Entities: Singular PascalCase (e.g., `Reservation`, `Account`, `Transaction`)
- DTOs: Java `record` with suffix `*Dto`, `*RequestDto`, `*ResponseDto`

## Architecture & Code Quality
- Layered architecture: `controller`, `service`, `repository`, `entity`, `dto`, `exception`, `config`.
- Constructor-based dependency injection (avoid field injection with `@Autowired`).
- Every public method must have updated and complete Javadoc documentation (`/** ... */`).
- Robust exception handling with `@RestControllerAdvice` and standard HTTP status codes (200, 201, 400, 404, 409, 500).
- Open-in-view disabled (`spring.jpa.open-in-view=false`) for transaction safety.

